00:00:02.240 --> 00:00:04.640 align:start position:0%
Egyptian security forces announced this  morning that they killed 40 suspected  militants following a roadside bomb  blast that left four people dead three  tourists from Vietnam and an Egyptian  guide were killed and at least 10 others  were injured Friday when the explosion  hit their tour bus near Egypt's Giza  pyramids Barry Peterson is in London  with the very latest very good morning  good morning although most of the  terrorists killed were in the area  around Giza authorities are not saying  if the raids were directly connected to  the bus attack the attack came at 6:15  in the evening about two and a half  miles from the Giza pyramids we heard a  big bang says this eyewitness and saw  people running investigators worked to  see how the bus was targeted and now  believed it was an improvised explosive  device attached to a wall detonated as  the bus went by the Vietnamese foreign  ministry issued an angry statement  saying it strongly condemned what had  called this act of terrorism Egypt's  Prime Minister visited the wounded and  hospitals and insisted there is no way  to stop terrorists but it isn't a  country in the world he said that is  100% safe from such a time terrorists  have attacked tourists in the past all  part of an effort to scare tourists away  and disrupt Egypt's lucrative tourism  industry Dana  Barry Petersen thanks Barry
 

